From: Azure Dreams <azuredreams@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:28:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Fast forward keeps the sound's pitch: time-stretch it
 instead of playing it faster

The game's speed no longer changes how fast the sound is played back. When the
game runs faster than normal, its audio is time-stretched to that speed (WSOLA:
short overlapping pieces, joined where their waveforms line up) before it's
queued, so music and sound effects stay at their pitch and in step with the
game. At normal speed the audio goes through untouched.
